<title>UK: BP, ARON KEEP BRENT CARGOES TURNING WET - TRADE.</title>
<headline>BP, ARON KEEP BRENT CARGOES TURNING WET - TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Both of the Brent cargoes turning wet from the paper chains on Tuesday were kept ahead of the five o'clock deadline, traders said.</p>
<p>BP and trading house J. Aron kept the cargoes, which were both due to load in the August 27-29 date range, the sources said.</p>
<p>One of the cargoes was originally an August 26-28 cargo that was clocked to Spanish refiner Repsol and then deferred.</p>
